WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:58.879
Iran is an Islamic republic that has

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:01.120
different layers of power.

00:00:58.879 --> 00:01:02.960
It means the president isn't fully in

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:06.320
charge. 

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:14.400
The ultimate authority in Iran is the

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:16.400
supreme leader and since 1989 that's

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.560
been Ayatollah Ali Khamenei.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.159
He oversees foreign policy and controls

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:22.320
powerful institutions

00:01:20.159 --> 00:01:24.159
like the judiciary, state media and

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:26.479
special forces known as the Islamic

00:01:24.159 --> 00:01:28.159
Revolutionary Guard Corps. The supreme

00:01:26.479 --> 00:01:30.079
leader is appointed by a group called

00:01:28.159 --> 00:01:32.720
the Assembly of Experts — as in

00:01:30.079 --> 00:01:34.479
experts in Islamic law. It's got 88

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.280
members who are elected every eight

00:01:34.479 --> 00:01:37.119
years.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.320
Then there's the elected president who

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:40.320
leads the government.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.920
He sets Iran's economic direction and

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.560
works with the supreme leader on

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:44.880
domestic

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.119
and foreign policy. There's also an

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.119
elected parliament that drafts laws.

00:01:47.119 --> 00:01:50.560
At the end of the day, though, the supreme

00:01:49.119 --> 00:01:52.960
leader can effectively

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:54.079
overrule all big decisions and when it

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:56.079
comes to elections

00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:57.920
there's another important institution

00:01:56.079 --> 00:02:01.439
involved — the Guardian Council.

00:02:12.879 --> 00:02:17.920
That means Iranian voters

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.879
can only choose from a preapproved list

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:21.440
of candidates

00:02:18.879 --> 00:02:23.360
and this year, out of almost 600 people

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:26.959
who applied to run for president,

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.959
only seven made the cut.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:31.040
Now, in the last few presidential

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.640
elections Iranians have had a clear

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.959
choice between a conservative

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:37.840
and a reformist but this year it's

00:02:34.959 --> 00:02:37.840
different.

00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:45.040
The Guardian Council hasn't approved any

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:47.040
reformist candidates that look like they

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:50.080
have a realistic chance of winning.

00:02:54.319 --> 00:02:57.360
So, who are the seven candidates? Well,

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.519
among them there's

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.599
Saeed Jalili. He's a senior figure in

00:02:59.519 --> 00:03:03.840
the hardline conservative camp

00:03:01.599 --> 00:03:06.400
and was Iran's chief nuclear negotiator

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:07.840
under President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.159
There's the former head of Iran's

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:12.560
central bank, Abdolnaser Hemmati.

00:03:10.159 --> 00:03:14.319
He's seen as a moderate candidate and so

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:16.800
is Mohsen Mehralizadeh

00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:18.800
who's standing as an independent. But the

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:20.159
man most people are talking about is

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.560
Ebrahim Raisi.

00:03:20.159 --> 00:03:23.440
He's widely seen as the frontrunner.

00:03:38.799 --> 00:03:43.519
So who is Ebrahim Raisi? He's a hardline

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:45.599
Islamic cleric who rose through the

00:03:43.519 --> 00:03:47.680
ranks as a prosecutor and judge.

00:03:45.599 --> 00:03:50.000
He ran in the last election and lost to

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.400
Rouhani but he got 38% of the

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.159
vote,

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.400
which helped to put him on the political

00:03:52.159 --> 00:03:54.400
map.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:58.159
For the last two years he's been head of

00:03:56.319 --> 00:03:58.560
the judiciary and is now being talked

00:03:58.159 --> 00:04:00.640
about

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:02.720
as a potential successor to the supreme

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:04.480
leader. In terms of policy

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:06.560
Raisi says he wants to develop the

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:08.400
domestic economy and improve relations

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:09.920
with countries like China and Russia.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:12.080
It's to help reduce the impact of

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:12.640
Western sanctions. He's also styled

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:15.120
himself

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.120
as a man of the people. 

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:43.440
But he's also got some serious

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:44.960
allegations hanging over him

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:47.520
linked to the mass execution of

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:49.360
political prisoners in 1988.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:51.040
Raisi is accused of being a member of

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:51.759
what was called a death commission in

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:53.759
Tehran

00:04:51.759 --> 00:04:54.880
while he was deputy prosecutor general.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:59.600
Now there's

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:00.320
one issue that's really dominating this

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.639
election

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.759
and that's the economy. Times are tough

00:05:02.639 --> 00:05:06.240
for people in Iran

00:05:03.759 --> 00:05:08.560
especially since 2018. That's when the

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.000
US reimposed sanctions after President

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:12.160
Trump pulled the Americans

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.160
out of an international deal to monitor

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.479
Iran's nuclear programme.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:17.199
In April of this year inflation hit 50

00:05:16.479 --> 00:05:18.800
percent.

00:05:17.199 --> 00:05:21.440
People are struggling to buy even the

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:23.520
basics, unemployment is also high and

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:26.720
COVID-19 has made things tougher.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:43.919
Now, a big factor for the economy is

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:44.560
going to be whether US sanctions are

00:05:43.919 --> 00:05:46.000
lifted

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:47.759
and that depends on whether they can

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.440
restore the nuclear deal

00:05:47.759 --> 00:05:51.520
with President Joe Biden in the White

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:53.360
House. The Americans and Iranians are

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:55.440
back at the negotiating table

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:57.199
but it's hard to say what might happen

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:58.960
if they don't reach a deal before

00:05:57.199 --> 00:06:01.919
President Rouhani leaves office in

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:04.720
August. 

00:06:22.319 --> 00:06:25.440
OK, but right now the big question in

00:06:24.479 --> 00:06:27.360
Iran is

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:29.520
just how many people are going to turn

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:31.440
up to vote. Last year's parliamentary

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:34.160
election had the lowest turnout since

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:36.400
the Islamic revolution in 1979

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:38.080
and a recent poll found that only around

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:39.600
38% of respondents

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:49.840
said they'll definitely vote in the

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:49.840
presidential election. 

00:07:09.759 --> 00:07:13.120
For Iran's leaders

00:07:11.039 --> 00:07:15.199
that's not a good look and the supreme

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:16.080
leader has urged people to come out and

00:07:15.199 --> 00:07:18.400
vote.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:19.759
Turnout says a lot about how much people

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:21.680
trust the system

00:07:19.759 --> 00:07:25.680
but right now it looks like a lot of

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:25.680
Iranians plan on staying at home.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:31.120
We'll have more coverage before and

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:32.880
after the Iranian elections on our

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:34.720
website aljazeera.com

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:36.720
and you can find more episodes of this

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:39.039
show on YouTube and social media —

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:45.840
just search for Start Here Al Jazeera.

00:07:39.039 --> 00:07:45.840
See you next week.

